    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\npairs\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nPairs supports registering a pair to `<BS>`. The `<C-h>` has the same functionality, but the plugin doesn't acknowledge for it. Similarly with `<C-w>` and `<C-u>`. I would like to see analogous behavior with regard to the other, mentioned keys.",
