        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I tested it, and it works, apart from one case that emerged which I didn't mention before. That is having `This (is|) an example.`, pressing `<C-u>` results in `|) an example.`, but `| an example.` is expected. Without looking into code, I assume that the plugin performs a one-character neighborhood check, as removing the bracket in situations like\r\n```\r\n{|\r\n    function();\r\n}\r\n```\r\nalso doesn't work this way with any key. Therefore, I consider this outside the scope of this issue, perhaps this plugin. Anyway, the current one has been solved, so thank you for the discussion and quick addressing. 😉",
